          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "кандидат (kandidát) was borrowed from Polish kandydat, from Latin candidātus (EtymDB) \"clothed in white\", since Roman candidates for office wore a white toga (Lewis & Short); the root is candidus \"white\"."
            }
          ]
        },
